      {
        "id": "segmented-arrows",
        "question": "Do the horizontal arrows of a segmented control (single-choice button row) swap in RTL?",
        "apg": "No segmented-control page. The radio group page names Right Arrow as next and is silent on RTL.",
        "libraries": [
          {
            "library": "ant-design",
            "behaviour": "Does not swap: ArrowLeft and ArrowUp always select the previous option, in both directions, although the component renders an -rtl class.",
            "evidence": "@rc-component/segmented es/index.js (handleKeyDown)",
            "checked": "source-read"
          },
          {
            "library": "material",
            "behaviour": "Swaps: ToggleButtonGroup passes isRtl to the roving tabindex root.",
            "evidence": "packages/mui-material/src/ToggleButtonGroup/ToggleButtonGroup.js",
            "checked": "source-read"
          },
          {
            "library": "radix",
            "behaviour": "Swaps: ToggleGroup resolves dir and hands it to the roving focus group.",
            "evidence": "packages/react/toggle-group/src/toggle-group.tsx",
            "checked": "source-read"
          },
          {
            "library": "react-aria",
            "behaviour": "Swaps for horizontal radio groups, the role a segmented control maps to.",
            "evidence": "packages/react-aria/src/radio/useRadioGroup.ts",
            "checked": "source-read"
          }
        ],
        "recommendation": "mirror-horizontal",
        "reason": "Same rule as every horizontal roving composite. The Ant Design behaviour sends ArrowLeft to the visually right-hand segment in RTL, which reads as a defect.",
